The bug was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was using `parts[1]` (the second element) instead of `parts[0]` (the first element) to return the first word. This caused:
1. `first_word('hello world')` to return 'world' instead of 'hello'
2. `first_word('solo')` to crash with an IndexError because there's no index 1 in a single-element list

The fix was simple: change `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]`.
